import{_ as t,o as s,c as a,a2 as r}from"./chunks/framework.BZO4qERu.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Workspace and history","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"guide/workspace.md","filePath":"guide/workspace.md","lastUpdated":1792570296000}'),n={name:"guide/workspace.md"};function o(i,e,d,l,c,h){return s(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[r('<h1 id="workspace-and-history" tabindex="-1">Workspace and history <a class="header-anchor" href="#workspace-and-history" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Workspace and history&quot;">​</a></h1><p>How the PaperSeek workspace is organized, where your data lives, and what survives a reload. For result-level tasks, see <a href="./results">Results and history</a>.</p><p>Open <strong>Search</strong>, <strong>Bibliometrics</strong>, or <strong>Reviews</strong> from the left sidebar. Use the module&#39;s history to reopen a saved search, analysis, or review.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Module</th><th>Subfunctions</th><th>Saved object</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Search</td><td>Search settings, Run progress, Results</td><td>One search run</td></tr><tr><td>Bibliometrics</td><td>Overview, Keywords, Paper relations, Data quality</td><td>One independent corpus analysis</td></tr><tr><td>Reviews</td><td>Papers, Outline, Draft, Citation evidence</td><td>One editable review</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The sidebar lists the current module’s history. The header button hides or shows the entire sidebar; on small screens it opens as a dismissible drawer. Use the new-record button to start a draft, the magnifying glass beside the history heading to search records, and <strong>All</strong> to open the current module’s full history list. A new draft is not a history record until it is saved or submitted.</p><p>The full history list provides record menus for rename, export, and delete. A title change does not rewrite the research question, review topic, or original execution settings. Deletion has a confirmation dialog. Active tasks cannot be deleted while they are running.</p><p>The sidebar footer contains <strong>Settings</strong>, documentation, and the account menu. Settings has four sections: <strong>Model APIs</strong>, <strong>Data sources</strong>, <strong>General</strong>, and <strong>User</strong>, at <code>/settings/models</code>, <code>/settings/sources</code>, <code>/settings/general</code>, and <code>/settings/user</code>. Return to a module through the sidebar or browser Back button.</p><p>Add or edit a model connection in its dialog and click <strong>Save</strong>. In a data-source configuration dialog, <strong>Save</strong> persists the key and options; <strong>Test connection</strong> also saves them before testing. A failed test or subsequently cancelling the dialog does not undo that save. Default model and ranking selections save when changed. They apply to new drafts; saved runs keep their execution settings. Review model settings apply to the current review and cannot change during generation. The <strong>User</strong> page shows the local data location and provides saved-key and history management. Language is available in General, the header, and the account menu; the online account menu also exposes account and service actions.</p><h2 id="inputs-saved-keys-and-browser-state" tabindex="-1">Inputs, saved keys, and browser state <a class="header-anchor" href="#inputs-saved-keys-and-browser-state" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Inputs, saved keys, and browser state&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Unsaved form inputs and drafts are temporary browser memory and disappear on reload. <strong>Test connection</strong> in the model connection dialog sends the draft to the server without saving it. In a data-source configuration dialog, the same action saves first; the input is then saved configuration, even if the test fails. <strong>Test</strong> and <strong>Test all</strong> in the source table use the configured credentials.</li><li>Saved model connections and data-source keys persist on the server. Community encrypts secret values in its database using the adjacent <code>credentials.master.key</code>; refreshing or restarting does not clear them. Settings returns key status and masked suffixes, not saved plaintext keys.</li><li>Submitted tasks may retain a separate encrypted credential copy for execution and recovery. <strong>Settings → User → Clear saved keys</strong> deletes saved connections and source keys, but does not affect already-submitted tasks.</li><li>Browser storage contains preferences such as language and sidebar visibility, not API keys. Clearing browser storage or reloading does not delete server-side keys.</li></ul><p>Citation maps are available under the review&#39;s <strong>Citation evidence → Paper relations</strong>. Old direct map and history links remain usable.</p><p>Switching modules retains loaded results, filters, selections, and scroll position in this browser session. The result cache keeps the ten most recently visited runs; reloading clears this temporary state. Unsaved outline and paragraph edits prompt before leaving, so you can keep editing or discard them. Save edits before reloading.</p><p>New reviews save the available source citation map with their evidence, so they can still show it after source-search deletion. Older reviews without that snapshot depend on the source record for this graph. Saved analyses always retain their own corpus snapshots.</p>',13)])])}const p=t(n,[["render",o]]);export{g as __pageData,p as default};
